<b>א.</b> "That he should awaken the dawn." The Shelah writes of the sod to connect day and night through Torah or prayer, both morning and evening.<br>
<br>
<b>ב.</b> "Because of." In any event, one should not quarrel with them (Beit Yosef).<br>
<br>
<b>ג.</b> "Immediately." Not literally at once; rather pause a little, as in Gittin 70a.
